<Chapter id="bgs">
<h2>Front RPC</h2>
  <p>Front carries Battle.net protobuf RPC before SC2 starts the Sunken service
  stream. The client contains protobuf descriptors for the services used here.</p>

  <h3 id="bgs-frame">RPC framing</h3>
  <p>The Base97563 client first opens TLS to the regional Front endpoint. The client
  then performs an RFC 6455 upgrade. The WebSocket subprotocol is
  <code>v1.rpc.battle.net</code>. One binary WebSocket message contains one Front
  RPC message.</p>
  <p>The server must select the same WebSocket subprotocol. A different or missing
  selection is rejected.</p>
  <figure class="diagram">
    <div class="wire-strip" aria-label="Front RPC message containing a two-byte header length, a protobuf header, and an optional protobuf body">
      <div class="segment tiny prefix"><b>2 bytes</b><br>header length<br><code>uint16_be</code></div>
      <div class="segment medium control"><b><code>header_length</code> bytes</b><br><code>bgs.protocol.Header</code></div>
      <div class="segment large payload"><b>remaining message bytes</b><br>protobuf body; can be empty</div>
    </div>
    <p class="chart-note">The length prefix gives only the protobuf header size.
    If <code>Header.size</code> is present, it must equal the body size. Base97563
    requests can omit this field.</p>
  </figure>
<pre is:raw><span class="syn-comment">offset  size                 description</span>
<span class="syn-comment">------  -------------------  ----------------------------------------------</span>
<span class="syn-number">0</span>       <span class="syn-number">2</span>                    header length, unsigned big-endian
<span class="syn-number">2</span>       <span class="syn-field">header_length</span>        protobuf <span class="syn-type">bgs.protocol.Header</span>
...     remainder of message protobuf request/response body

<span class="syn-type">uint16_be</span> <span class="syn-field">header_length</span>
<span class="syn-type">bytes</span>     <span class="syn-field">header</span>[header_length]
<span class="syn-type">bytes</span>     <span class="syn-field">body</span>[websocket_message_end - current_offset]
</pre>
  <p>The WebSocket message sets the frame boundary. <code>Header.size</code>
  validates the body byte count when present.</p>
  <p>The WebSocket library applies RFC 6455 client masking. The Front decoder receives
  the unmasked binary-message payload. Server messages arrive unmasked.</p>
  <p>An empty or truncated Front header is rejected. WebSocket messages are limited
  to 16 MiB.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Header field</th><th>Protobuf wire type</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1 <code>service_id</code></td><td>varint</td><td>Numeric dispatch value. The first Connect uses 0. Responses use <code>0xfe</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2 <code>method_id</code></td><td>varint</td><td>Method number within the selected service.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3 <code>token</code></td><td>varint</td><td>Request/callback correlation token.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4 <code>object_id</code></td><td>varint</td><td>Optional addressed service object.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5 <code>size</code></td><td>varint</td><td>Body byte count.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>6 <code>status</code></td><td>varint</td><td>RPC result/status code.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>7 <code>error</code></td><td>length-delimited, repeated</td><td>Structured error details.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>8 <code>timeout</code></td><td>varint</td><td>Optional request timeout.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>9 <code>is_response</code></td><td>varint boolean</td><td>Explicit response marker when present.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>10 <code>forward_targets</code></td><td>length-delimited, repeated</td><td>Optional process forwarding targets.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>11 <code>service_hash</code></td><td>fixed32</td><td>FNV-1a hash of the full protobuf service name. Protobuf fixed32 is little-endian on the wire.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>13 <code>client_id</code></td><td>length-delimited UTF-8</td><td>Optional client identifier.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>14 <code>fanout_target</code></td><td>length-delimited, repeated</td><td>Optional structured fanout targets.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>15 <code>client_id_fanout_target</code></td><td>length-delimited UTF-8, repeated</td><td>Optional client-ID fanout targets.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>16 <code>client_record</code></td><td>length-delimited bytes</td><td>Optional opaque client record.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3 id="bgs-dispatch">Dispatch and callbacks</h3>
  <p>The service and method fields select the operation. The token identifies the
  related call. These functions are independent.</p>
  <BgsDispatchDiagram />
  <p>Each request sets <code>service_id=0</code> and uses the 32-bit FNV-1a hash of
  the full protobuf service name. This rule includes the first Connect request.</p>
<pre is:raw><span class="syn-field">h</span> = <span class="syn-number">0x811c9dc5</span>
<span class="syn-keyword">for each</span> <span class="syn-type">UTF-8 byte</span> b <span class="syn-keyword">in</span> full_service_name:
    <span class="syn-field">h</span> = h <span class="syn-keyword">XOR</span> b
    <span class="syn-field">h</span> = (h * <span class="syn-number">0x01000193</span>) <span class="syn-keyword">AND</span> <span class="syn-number">0xffffffff</span>
</pre>
  <p>Relevant names include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>bnet.protocol.connection.ConnectionService</code></li>
    <li><code>bnet.protocol.authentication.AuthenticationServer</code></li>
    <li><code>bnet.protocol.authentication.AuthenticationClient</code></li>
    <li><code>bnet.protocol.challenge.ChallengeNotify</code></li>
    <li><code>bnet.protocol.game_utilities.GameUtilities</code></li>
    <li><code>bnet.protocol.account.AccountService</code></li>
    <li><code>bnet.protocol.session.SessionService</code> and <code>SessionListener</code></li>
  </ul>
  <p>A server-to-client call uses a listener service. If the descriptor declares a
  response, the client must send a response. Set <code>service_id</code> to
  <code>0xfe</code>. Copy the callback token. Set the status to zero.</p>
  <p>If the return type is <code>NO_RESPONSE</code>, the client omits the response
  frame. An empty declared response still requires a response frame.</p>
  <p>The authentication loop dispatches callbacks while its request tokens are
  pending. Outside that loop, only <code>ConnectionService.Echo</code> is handled
  automatically. Any other unexpected callback is rejected.</p>

  <h3 id="bgs-logon">Logon sequence</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Direction</th><th>Service / method</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1</td><td>C&rarr;S</td><td>ConnectionService / 1</td><td>Use <code>service_id=0</code>, <code>token=0</code>, and the ConnectionService hash. Advertise bindless RPC.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2</td><td>C&rarr;S</td><td>AuthenticationServer / 1</td><td>Send program <code>S2</code>, platform <code>Mc64</code>, locale <code>enUS</code>, the embedded SDK identity, and <code>application_version=0</code>. A cached credential is optional.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3</td><td>S&rarr;C</td><td>ChallengeNotify / 3</td><td>Send an external <code>web_auth_url</code> challenge when necessary. The method is <code>NO_RESPONSE</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4</td><td>local HTTPS</td><td>Battle.net account flow</td><td>When challenged, cookies, MFA, CAPTCHA, and account state stay in the web view.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5</td><td>C&rarr;S</td><td>AuthenticationServer / 7</td><td>Submit the short-lived credential from the web flow.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>6</td><td>S&rarr;C</td><td>AuthenticationClient / 5</td><td><code>LogonResult</code>: account, game accounts, region, and 64-byte session key.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>7</td><td>C&rarr;S</td><td>AuthenticationServer / 8</td><td>Generate a new cached credential. Replace the accepted cached credential.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>8</td><td>C&rarr;S</td><td>GameUtilities / 1</td><td>Start the SC2 Front bootstrap directly after authentication.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>For Base97563, <code>LogonRequest.version</code> contains this exact embedded SDK
  identity:</p>
<pre is:raw><span class="syn-string">Battle.net Game Service SDK v1.48.2 "cf68e241e0"/104 (Jul 14 2026 19:45:54)</span></pre>
  <p>Protobuf field 6, <code>application_version</code>, is zero. Use the embedded
  SDK identity and this fixed field value independently of the installation build
  number.</p>
  <p>Authentication callbacks can occur between RPC responses. Method 10 reports a
  logon update. Method 14 reports game-account selection. Methods 11 through 13 are
  <code>NO_RESPONSE</code>. The client must dispatch these methods as callbacks.</p>
  <p>The web view handles only the account challenge. The Front connection remains
  the protocol client. The client submits the short-lived credential with
  AuthenticationServer method 7.</p>
  <p>The cached credential from method 8 and the short-lived challenge credential
  are separate values. A cached credential can prevent the next web challenge.
  Replace it after successful use. If the server rejects it, start the web
  challenge.</p>

  <h3 id="game-utilities">Sunken session request</h3>
  <p>The client sends <code>GameUtilities.ProcessClientRequest</code> method 1. The
  <code>ClientRequest</code> contains only the required fields. Top-level field 1
  contains typed attributes. Top-level field 4 contains the first SC2 game-account
  entity from <code>LogonResult</code>.</p>
  <p>The later game-account selection callback is validated. The request continues
  to use the first entity from <code>LogonResult</code>.</p>
  <p>The request omits the host-process, Battle.net-account, program, and client-info
  fields.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Attribute name</th><th>Variant type</th><th>Current value shape</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>LogonTokenRequest</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>"0.0.1"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>environment</code></td><td>string</td><td>Regional environment string; <code>"US"</code> for this target.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>session_key</code></td><td>blob</td><td>64 private bytes from <code>LogonResult</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>locale</code></td><td>string</td><td><code>"enUS"</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>An Attribute contains protobuf field 1, <code>name</code>. It also contains
  protobuf field 2, <code>Variant</code>. The following field numbers select the
  Variant type:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>2: Boolean</li>
    <li>3: signed integer</li>
    <li>4: double</li>
    <li>5: string</li>
    <li>6: blob</li>
    <li>7: embedded message</li>
    <li>8: FourCC string</li>
    <li>9: unsigned integer</li>
    <li>10: entity ID</li>
  </ul>
  <p>A successful response contains another attribute set. The handoff requires
  these attributes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>address</code>: native endpoint string;</li>
    <li><code>session_key</code>: exactly 64 private bytes;</li>
    <li><code>account_region</code>: unsigned integer in 0..255;</li>
    <li><code>game_account_name</code> and <code>account_mail</code>: private identity strings;</li>
    <li><code>logon_response</code>: a bit-packed native <code>LogonResponse3</code>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>These attributes transfer the session from Front to Sunken. The
  handoff section defines their use.</p>
  <BackToContents />
</Chapter>
